(P101.macro: BitZero V2 Z zero only. Sets Z of the active WCS.)
(Call: G65 P101 Z<t> R<r>)
(Z = mm from the plate base to the plate top face. Measure it.)
(R = optional. Maximum Z search in mm. The default is 15.)
(Carbide 3D does not publish the thickness. See README.md.)
(Start: the BitZero flat on the stock top, the pin tip above a flat spot)
(of the top face, not above the bore, less than R mm above it.)
(Needs: grblHAL with EXPR, and a homed machine.)
(Probe input: DEFAULT, the BitZero. G38.2 has no P word here.)

o200 if [#26 LE 0]
  (abort, P101 needs Z more than 0. See README.md)
o200 endif
o201 if [#<_homed_state> EQ 0]
  (abort, P101 needs a homed machine)
o201 endif

M73
G21 G91 G94
G65 P5 Q0

#<seek> = 100
#<slow> = 25
#<bnd> = 15
o202 if [#18 GT 0]
  #<bnd> = #18
o202 endif

(Soft limit check. Machine Z is 0 at the home end, negative downward.)
G65 P1 Q132
#<zmin> = [0 - #<_value>]
o203 if [[#<_abs_z> - #<bnd>] LT [#<zmin> + 1]]
  (abort, P101 Z probe can go past the Z soft limit)
o203 endif

#<nz> = [0 - #<bnd>]
G38.2 Z#<nz> F#<seek>
G0 Z1
G38.2 Z-2 F#<slow>
G10 L20 P0 Z#26

(Safe Z: 5 mm up, then G53 Z-5. Home Z is -$27 = -3, machine_limits.c:157-159.)
G0 Z5
G90
G53 G0 Z-5
(MSG, P101 done: Z zero set on the stock top. Remove the clip.)
M99
